# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local database
ecosystem.db
# ...and the timestamped copies a migration takes before touching it. `ecosystem.db`
# above is an exact name, not a glob, so a backup was landing in `git status` as an
# untracked 13MB file waiting for somebody to `git add .`
#
# `bak-` was not enough: the migration scripts name their copies after what they are
# about to change - ecosystem.db.pre-regions.1787585683, ecosystem.db.pre-dex.*,
# ecosystem.db.pre-translations.* - and ten of those, 13 to 26MB each, were sitting in
# `git status` for exactly the reason the paragraph above describes. The glob covers
# every one of them, including their `-shm` and `-wal` companions, whose names end in
# `-shm` rather than `.db-shm` and so slip past the patterns below.
ecosystem.db.*
ecosystem.db.bak-*
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# One-off migration scripts
migrate_genders.py

# Sprite assets (fetched separately from PokeAPI/sprites). Anchored to the repo root
# with a leading slash: unanchored, `KyuSprites/` would also swallow a directory of that
# name nested anywhere else, which is a wider promise than this entry means to make.
# Now ~1GB, since pollute.py's corrupted variants live under it too.
/KyuSprites/

# Trainer sprites for the profile card. 650 files, same provenance as KyuSprites and
# ignored for the same reason: fetched art, not source. Root-anchored for the same
# reason as above.
/trainers/

# Local battle backdrops (only consumed by the scratch battletest cog)
assets/

# Scratch/experimental cog, kept local
cogs/battletest.py

# Battle-engine test suites, kept local (run with: python tests/run_all.py)
tests/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Editor / tooling
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
